      "writtenOn": "2020-08-18T05:51:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "if we have one RT pinned thread and 100 fair tasks, we end up calling pick_next_task() and put_prev_task() on that RT task 100 times. So one pinned thread is enough to cause overhead, I think.\n\nCan we try bookmarking the class (next\u0027s sched_class) here so that we can start from that class instead of for_each_classes()?\n\nwould it be too much to add an argument to pick_next_task() to skip pinned kthread? I like bookmarking since we don\u0027t have to duplicate the pinned kthread checks in all scheduling classes.",
      "parentUuid": "757100ae_220a7c15",
